  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.74,
            0.047,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Quadrilaterals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.087,
            0.326,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 1,
              "bbox": [
                0.131,
                0.087,
                0.326,
                0.299
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_1.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.376,
            0.139,
            0.845,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can compute the four angles between the diagonals to be x, x, 180 – x, and 180 – x."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.376,
            0.181,
            0.679,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you find the other angles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.309,
            0.651,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since we know that ∆AOB is isosceles, we can denote the measures of both of its base angles by a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.356,
            0.625,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the value of a (in degrees) in terms of x? We have,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.406,
            0.491,
            0.423
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "a+a+x=180"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.424,
            0.614,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(sum of the interior angles of a triangle)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.357,
            0.453,
            0.48,
            0.473
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "2 a = 1 8 0 - x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.479,
            0.517,
            0.509
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "a = \\frac{(180 - x)}{2} = 90 - \\frac{x}{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.696,
            0.306,
            0.88,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.696,
                0.306,
                0.88,
                0.503
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.515,
            0.696,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, in the isosceles ∆AOD, let the base angles be b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.398,
            0.539,
            0.601,
            0.559
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "b+b+180-x=180"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.325,
            0.568,
            0.514,
            0.59
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "2b = 180 - (180 - x)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.331,
            0.597,
            0.508,
            0.619
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "2b = 180 - 180 + x"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.386,
            0.627,
            0.454,
            0.648
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "2b = \\overline{x}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.664,
            0.449,
            0.69
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { b = \\frac { X } { 2 }   . } \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.696,
            0.661,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All the angles of the quadrilateral are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a + b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , which is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.732,
            0.49,
            0.759
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "9 0 - { \\frac { x } { 2 } } + { \\frac { x } { 2 } } = 9 0 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.692,
            0.587,
            0.88,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 19,
              "bbox": [
                0.692,
                0.587,
                0.88,
                0.803
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_19.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.764,
            0.684,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, all four angles of the quadrilateral ABCD are 90°. What can we say about AB and CD, and AD and BC?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.812,
            0.848,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta  AOB  \\cong \\Delta  COD"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta AOD \\cong \\Delta COB"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Hence, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{AB} = \\mathrm{CD}_{:}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{AD} = \\mathrm{CB}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " since they are the corresponding parts of congruent triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
